<!--
Deep Ocean: the surface, and the water under it.

  Still no fish, no shell, no anchor — the old note was right that water has no
  silhouette and the honest drawing of it is its surface. What it was missing is
  depth: three identical parallel waves are the clip-art version of that idea.
  These shorten and flatten as they fall away, which is what turns a stack of
  lines into distance, and a bubble trail rises through them.

  A curling swell was tried and abandoned. A long curved mass with a rounded end
  and a dot above it is a body with an eye — it read as a whale, and once seen
  it cannot be unseen. Nothing in this mark closes.

  Drawn in white and tinted at the call site with the zone's own ZoneAccent.
-->
